# The trial of pod-opentunnel in podssh (T-033; call C603), at podssh's main
# b9c04657 (pod-opentunnel.commit), after the patch of pod-piping
# (pod-opentunnel.needs). crates/podssh-relay/src/opentunnel/ becomes a
# module of `pub use pod_opentunnel::*` and podssh's ENV
# (PODSSH_OPENTUNNEL); pinggy, localtunnel, hostc and bore take its dials'
# types. podssh-cli gives the dials podssh's way out
# (podssh_ws::client::way of the proxy of the environment), the API its
# user agent, the node its provider (podssh_ws::tls::context) and the
# record podssh's places. The tests of the road, its plant t530 and the
# workflows opentunnel-interop.yml and opentunnel-live.yml leave podssh;
# tests/opentunnel_stand_in/ stays, as the CLI tests take it by path. The
# steps: the record with its citations, the repository checks; no moved
# file stays; the crate in the tree; the library with each road that takes
# its dials, with its unit tests of them; the CLI and its tests of the road
# (opentunnel_road, funnel_opentunnel, with the stand-in); rustfmt of the
# crates that the patch changes; the test targets of the gate.
cargo run -q -p podssh-todo -- remap Cargo.lock > /dev/null
cargo run -q -p podssh-todo -- check
python3 scripts/check-repo.py
test ! -e crates/podssh-relay/src/opentunnel && test ! -e crates/podssh-relay/tests/opentunnel_link.rs && test ! -e scripts/plants/t530-tunnel-not-kept.plant
cargo tree -q -p podssh-relay --features opentunnel -i pod-opentunnel | grep -q '^pod-opentunnel v'
cargo clippy -q --all-targets -p podssh-relay --all-features -- -D warnings -A clippy::collapsible_if
cargo test -q -p podssh-relay --features opentunnel,pinggy,serveo,localtunnel,hostc,bore --lib -- pinggy localtunnel hostc bore opentunnel
cargo clippy -q --all-targets -p podssh-cli -p podssh-iroh -- -D warnings -A clippy::collapsible_if
cargo test -q -p podssh-cli --lib opentunnel
cargo test -q -p podssh-cli --test opentunnel_road --test funnel_opentunnel
cargo fmt -p podssh-relay -p podssh-cli --check
python3 -I "$PODCRATES/scripts/check-consumer-toolchains.py"
python3 -I "$PODCRATES/scripts/check-consumer-tests.py"
